{
 "_readme": "Shared cases for the plugin's handling of the tracker's answer to get_workflow_for_item, run by scripts/tests/run-workflow-fetch.sh. builtin is the definition the entry skill supplies; context is the start context; server is what the tracker's own checks need to agree with them; answers are sample answers in the tracker's response shape (match, ignoredOverride, skills, organizationId), each with the definition the runner must pin (definitionSource), the short fallback code it keeps (fallbackReason, null for an organization run) and, for a definition the plugin deliberately refuses, the validation code (invalidCode). Every sample's definition id is its workflowId, and every sample's hash is the canonical hash of its definition except the one changed after hashing, which keeps the hash it had before the change. Example hosts and names only.",
 "builtin": {
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "claim-only",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Claim only",
  "startsWhen": "item-picked-up",
  "endsBy": null,
  "appliesTo": {
   "workTypes": [],
   "tags": [],
   "repositories": []
  },
  "minPluginVersion": "4.2.0",
  "phases": [
